{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"I’ve locked the main dimension table. Axes are X across the cover, Y along its 250 mm length, and Z from the open rim to the roof.\n\n| Feature | Dimensions / positions (mm) |\n|---|---|\n| Envelope | X 327, Y 250, Z 175 |\n| Body profile | 300 wide; 45° roof shoulders; R15 transitions; 7.50 rim thickness |\n| Shell | 1.50 minimum wall; 2.00 exterior pocket depth |\n| Rim holes | 12; Ø5 with Ø6.05 counterbores; indicated depths 7.50 and 1.80 |\n| Rim hole centres | X ±156.50 at Y −88, 0, 88; Y ±117 at X −88, 0, 88 |\n| Roof bosses | 8 M4; X −86, 0, 79 at Y 79.50; X −86, −6 at Y 9.50; X −86, 4, 79 at Y −84.50 |\n| Side mounting bosses | 6 M4; X ±137; Y 56.50, −34.50, −70 |\n| End recess field | 18 columns, 15 pitch, 9 width; end heights 119.67, 134.06, 152.11 |\n| Side recess field | Four pairs per side; 8 web width, 30° diagonal; 44 height, 13.50 gap, 15 end margin |\n| Other relief | Roof boss projection 9.11; roof/end offset 14; radii R4, R7, R10 and R15 |\n\nStacked-span checks: the 175 dimension runs from the open rim face to the exterior roof, so it already includes the roof. The 90 dimension runs from that same rim face to the side-boss tip: `boss_tip_Z = 90`, not `175 + 90`. The 327 dimension spans both flange extremes: `327 = 300 + 2 × 13.5`. The 250 plan dimension spans both end faces: `250 = 125 + 125`. Recessed wall regions retain 1.5 mm, so the unrecessed wall is modeled as `1.5 + 2 = 3.5 mm`.\n\nThe tiny end-wall threaded callout is not sufficiently clear to locate reliably; I’ll preserve the visible mounting features without inventing another hole pattern.\n"}}
